WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.267
OT architecture should make communication deliberate.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:10.454
The Purdue model is a useful mental model for discussing layers of an industrial environment.

00:00:10.454 --> 00:00:16.335
At lower levels are the physical process, sensors, actuators, and basic control.

00:00:16.335 --> 00:00:20.473
Above them are supervisory systems and operations management.

00:00:20.473 --> 00:00:28.967
Enterprise services sit higher, with an industrial demilitarized zone, or industrial DMZ, often separating business and operational networks.

00:00:28.967 --> 00:00:34.412
The model is not a perfect map of every modern facility.

00:00:34.412 --> 00:00:40.729
Cloud services, wireless devices, vendor connections, and distributed sites can cross traditional boundaries.

00:00:40.729 --> 00:00:50.965
Its value is that it forces teams to ask which functions belong together, where trust changes, and which communications are actually required.

00:00:50.965 --> 00:00:57.717
Segmentation limits unnecessary connectivity between enterprise IT, operations systems, control networks, and field devices.

00:00:57.717 --> 00:01:07.518
A well-designed boundary permits documented business flows while reducing the ability of an incident to move directly toward critical control assets.

00:01:07.518 --> 00:01:15.577
Rules should be based on known sources, destinations, protocols, and operational purpose rather than broad network access.

00:01:15.577 --> 00:01:27.991
An industrial DMZ can host services that exchange information across the IT and OT boundary, such as patch staging, remote-access gateways, replication services, or intermediary data transfer.

00:01:27.991 --> 00:01:33.436
This avoids direct connections from ordinary enterprise endpoints to control systems.

00:01:33.436 --> 00:01:37.574
The DMZ is not protective by name alone.

00:01:37.574 --> 00:01:45.197
Services must be hardened, monitored, maintained, and configured so they do not become an uncontrolled bridge.

00:01:45.197 --> 00:01:48.029
Segmentation also applies within OT.

00:01:48.029 --> 00:01:55.216
Separate sites, production cells, safety-related functions, and management interfaces when risk and operations justify it.

00:01:55.216 --> 00:02:02.839
Avoid assuming that every device on an internal control network should communicate with every other device.

00:02:02.839 --> 00:02:09.591
At the same time, changes must preserve required timing, redundancy, troubleshooting, and failover behavior.

00:02:09.591 --> 00:02:12.858
The practical objective is controlled connectivity.

00:02:12.858 --> 00:02:21.352
Maintain current diagrams, document approved flows, monitor boundary traffic, review temporary access, and test rule changes with engineers.

00:02:21.352 --> 00:02:28.539
Good architecture reduces exposure and creates useful detection points without making the physical operation brittle.
